// Pashto (ps) — Eastern Iranian, Perso-Arabic ABJAD (extended). wikipron pus (human) PRIMARY + kaikki pus (human)
// SECONDARY. Like Urdu/Persian, SHORT vowels are usually unwritten → folded (unrecoverable): a~ə~i~u default-vowel
// quality. Also folds: dental t̪~t / retroflex notation, r~ɻ, the NARROW→BROAD ښ/ږ notation (ʂ~ʃ, ʐ~ʒ), and length.
//
// ⚠ EVERY PASHTO REFEREE WE HAVE IS A MACROLANGUAGE AGGREGATE, AND THIS ENGINE IS ONE VARIETY. ISO 639-3 `pus`
// is a macrolanguage — pbt (Southern/Kandahari), pbu (Northern/Peshawar), pst (Central/Waziri) — and wikipron,
// kaikki and espeak-ng's ps_list are all aggregated over it. `pashto.ts` declares a single variety ("ښ/ږ =
// Kandahari retroflex ʂ/ʐ"), so the umbrella marks a correct Southern reading wrong wherever the aggregate
// happens to carry only a Northern one. ⚠ AND THE FOLDS CANNOT PAPER OVER IT: merging the Northern x (ښ) or
// ɡ (ږ) into our ʂ/ʐ would also merge خ and ګ, which are real phoneme contrasts. Only the NARROW→BROAD
// notation folds are legitimate (ʂ→ʃ, ʐ→ʒ), and those are what remain below.
//
// So the primary DELIBERATELY STAYS THE AGGREGATE — it is the honest floor and must not be gamed — and the
// variety slices sit beside it as secondaries, cut by tools/pashto/split_referee_by_dialect.py on the ښ/ږ
// isogloss alone (ښ→ʂ/x/ç, ږ→ʐ/ɡ/ʝ; a broad ʃ/ʒ is UNCOMMITTED and stays in every slice).
//
// ⚠ THE VALIDATION IS THE HIT COUNT, NOT THE PERCENTAGE. A variety filter must not remove anything the engine
// was already scoring; if it does, it is a difficulty filter wearing a linguistic label. Ours: 744 → 744 on
// wikipron and 666 → 666 on kaikki, so the whole gain is denominator. And the engine scores HIGHEST on its own
// variety — pbt 63.0% / pst 60.4% / pbu 58.1% — which is the second check that the slices are real.
//
// ⚠ THE AGGREGATE LEANS NORTHERN, WHICH IS THE REAL REASON THE UMBRELLA SCORE IS LOW. Counting the isogloss
// across the primary: ښ is x(pbu) 138 · ʃ(broad) 99 · ʂ(pbt) 52 · ç(pst) 32, and ږ is ɡ(pbu) 151 · ʒ 84 ·
// ʐ(pbt) 28 · ʝ(pst) 12. kaikki is the same shape (x 90 / ʂ 21, ɡ 119 / ʐ 17). So a SOUTHERN engine is being
// graded against a reference that answers Northern roughly 3:1 on the diagnostic letters — the umbrella is
// not a neutral average, it is mostly another variety.
//
// ⚠ AND CENTRAL IS BARELY ATTESTED AT ALL (ç ×32 / ʝ ×12 in wikipron, ×2 / ×0 in kaikki). `ps.*-pst.tsv`
// therefore is NOT a usable Central referee: almost everything in it is variety-neutral material that every
// slice carries. It is emitted for completeness and to make the absence visible; do not read a pst score as
// evidence about Waziri.
{
    "referees": [
        { "file": "ps.wikipron-pus-broad.tsv", "source": "wikipron pus_arab broad (human) — MACROLANGUAGE aggregate, the honest floor", "role": "primary" },
        { "file": "ps.kaikki-pus.tsv", "source": "kaikki pus (Wiktionary, human)", "role": "secondary" },
        { "file": "ps.wikipron-pbt.tsv", "source": "wikipron pus → pbt (Southern) slice — our variety, 744/1181 = 63.0%", "role": "secondary" },
        { "file": "ps.kaikki-pbt.tsv", "source": "kaikki pus → pbt (Southern) slice — our variety, 666/1010 = 65.9%", "role": "secondary" },
        { "file": "ps.kaikki-kandahari.tsv", "source": "kaikki pus KANDAHARI slice (hand-cut, 95 rows — superseded in size by ps.kaikki-pbt.tsv)", "role": "secondary" }
    ],
    "segmentJoin": true,
    "folds": [
        {
            "pattern": "(.)\\1",
            "replace": "$1",
            "note": "geminate as length ː (ours) vs doubled symbol (referee) — notation (as pa)"
        },
        { "pattern": "t̪", "replace": "t", "note": "dental ⟨ت/ط/د⟩ notation (referee-variable)" },
        { "pattern": "d̪", "replace": "d", "note": "dental notation" },
        { "pattern": "[əaiu]", "replace": "ə", "note": "SHORT vowel quality a~ə~i~u — UNRECOVERABLE from the undiacritized abjad (the deferred restoration subsystem)" },
        { "pattern": "ɪ", "replace": "ə", "note": "referee short ɪ = our default short vowel" },
        { "pattern": "ʊ", "replace": "ə", "note": "referee short ʊ = default short vowel" },
        { "pattern": "ʂ", "replace": "ʃ", "note": "ښ: our narrow Kandahari ʂ vs the referee's BROAD ʃ — a transcription-granularity fold, not a dialect one. ⚠ `ç` was REMOVED from this class on 2026-08-10: it is the CENTRAL/Waziri reflex, so folding it in merged pbt with pst — a dialect merge hiding inside a notation rule. MEASURED IMPACT: ZERO, on every referee. Central-only entries are rare (ç ×32 in wikipron, ×2 in kaikki) and the ones that exist also list a ʂ or broad-ʃ variant, which still credits us. Kept because it is right in principle and costs nothing, and stated as zero-impact so nobody re-derives it as a win." },
        { "pattern": "ʐ", "replace": "ʒ", "note": "ږ: our narrow ʐ vs the referee's broad ʒ — notation only. Unlike the ښ rule above this one never merged dialects: the Northern ɡ and Central ʝ are untouched by it, so it stays as written." },
        { "pattern": "[ɻɽ]", "replace": "r", "note": "retroflex flap ⟨ړ⟩ ɻ ~ r notation" }
    ]
}
